| `requirement traceability` | A requirement is a heading in a `kind: spec` document that opens with an id, and a numbered criterion is a `- AC-<n>: <text>` line below it. A test names one with `@pytest.mark.req("<id>")`. Each criterion, or requirement that has none, is `covered`, a `gap` with a reason, or `uncovered`, and a bare requirement id never covers numbered criteria. The id prefixes are a closed config list, and an unlisted prefix is refused. | `make trace`; `make test` | [`traceability.id_prefixes`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`traceability.marker`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`traceability.gaps`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`traceability.no_requirements`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Reads marker calls from source, so `make trace` does not see a marker reached through a name other than `pytest.mark` or an imported `mark`, and a test's assertions are not judged; the gate test compares the reading with pytest's own collection. Not test coverage of code. | [README.md](../specs/README.md) | always |
